From 2f5d49e5a976e2a551008d49fa242451ac925913 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:18:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] video: preserve independent source HDR diagnostic records

Expose original HDR10 BL, DV L6/L1 and HDR10+ records, plus the actual peak detector, without changing renderer metadata or equality. Preserve through copies, AVFrame round trips and dual-track pairing. Let the mpv-ht adapter supply compact shared source rows to native Stats. Add a native copy/round-trip/equality test.
---
 DOCS/man/input.rst           | 43 ++++++++++++++++++
 filters/f_enhancement_pair.c |  6 +++
 player/command.c             | 27 ++++++++++++
 player/lua/stats.lua         | 14 ++++++
 test/meson.build             |  5 +++
 test/source_hdr.c            | 85 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 video/mp_image.c             | 54 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 video/mp_image.h             | 16 +++++++
 video/out/vo_gpu_next.c      |  1 +
 9 files changed, 251 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 test/source_hdr.c

diff --git a/DOCS/man/input.rst b/DOCS/man/input.rst
index bf8377c1e..272168c4d 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/input.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/input.rst
@@ -2980,6 +2980,49 @@ Property list
         This uses the configured ``--hdr-peak-percentile`` and peak-detection
         black cutoff, but is reported before temporal smoothing.
 
+    ``video-params/source-hdr-metadata-version``
+        Version of the independent original source records below (currently 1).
+        Diagnostic only; these values do not affect rendering. The existing
+        ``min-luma``, ``max-luma`` and dynamic fields remain renderer metadata
+        and may combine multiple authorities. Prefer ``video-out-params`` for
+        the paired BL/EL frame in dual-track Dolby Vision.
+
+    ``video-params/source-hdr10-mdl-present``, ``video-params/source-hdr10-cll-present``
+        Whether the original base-layer mastering display and content light
+        records were present. Values are in ``source-hdr10-min``,
+        ``source-hdr10-max``, ``source-hdr10-max-cll`` and
+        ``source-hdr10-max-fall``, in cd/m². Missing records make their numeric
+        fields unavailable. Zero CLL/FALL means unspecified, not a zero peak.
+
+    ``video-params/source-dovi-present``
+        Dolby Vision metadata was supplied by the decoder. Parsed Level 6 and
+        Level 1 records have separate ``source-dovi-l6-present`` and
+        ``source-dovi-l1-present`` flags; raw RPU presence alone does not
+        imply these parsed values are available.
+
+    ``video-params/source-dovi-l6-min``, ``video-params/source-dovi-l6-max``
+        Original Level 6 mastering display minimum/maximum in cd/m². The
+        minimum is converted from units of 0.0001 cd/m². These are NOT the
+        RPU source_min_pq/source_max_pq fields. Level 6 light levels are
+        ``source-dovi-l6-max-cll`` and ``source-dovi-l6-max-fall`` in cd/m².
+
+    ``video-params/source-dovi-l1-min-pq``, ``video-params/source-dovi-l1-max-pq``, ``video-params/source-dovi-l1-avg-pq``
+        Original authored Level 1 codes divided by 4095 (normalized PQ, 0–1),
+        before peak detection can replace renderer values. Zero is valid.
+
+    ``video-params/source-hdr10plus-present``
+        Whether an original HDR10+ record was supplied. Its MaxSCL components
+        are ``source-hdr10plus-max-r``, ``source-hdr10plus-max-g`` and
+        ``source-hdr10plus-max-b``; average maxRGB is
+        ``source-hdr10plus-avg``. All are in cd/m², not CIE Y Level 1 values.
+        These and the DV records remain separate if both formats are present.
+
+    ``video-params/measured-metric``
+        Detector accompanying the returned peak measurements: ``standard``
+        (CIE Y), ``bt2020-rgb`` (P), or ``maxrgb-rgb`` (maxRGB). Available only
+        with a valid detector result. This is not a requested option or an
+        output-pixel measurement. The detector does not report a minimum.
+
     ``video-params/raw-avg-pq-y``
         Unsmoothed average CIE Y of the current measured frame (in PQ, 0-1).
 
